        "en": "Anyway, that's enough background on how I fell in love with reading. It's time to explore how reading has the power to change your brain. It's so intuitive that before we begin reading, we look at shapes and patterns on the page. After that, the back of the brain receives these images and processes them. They proceed to the temporal lobe next, which sits behind the ears and is most commonly associated with processing auditory information and memory encoding.",
